title: "Mini-JEPA"
message: "If you use this software or cite these results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "sjyu0423"
    alias: "sjyu0423"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sjyu0423/Mini_JEPA"
url: "https://sjyu0423.github.io/Mini_JEPA/"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
abstract: >-
  Mini-JEPA is a compact, reproducible research project that investigates whether
  a joint-embedding predictive architecture can learn useful motion representations
  from synthetic bouncing-ball video without reconstructing pixels or receiving
  physical-state labels during self-supervised training.
keywords:
  - self-supervised learning
  - JEPA
  - representation learning
  - visual motion
  - bouncing ball
  - PyTorch
